<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμόφων-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speaking the same language
				with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθνεα οὐκ ὁ. σφίσι</span> (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλοις</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.98
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.4.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of the same sound</i> or <i>tone, in unison with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τισι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				158
			</span></i>(lyr.). Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>
			<i>having the same name with,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.2.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in Music,
				<i>on the same note, in unison,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμφωνος</span> (in concord), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				921a7
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Nicom.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				11.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως</span>”
				<i>with one voice (accord),</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Galb.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				3.239
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>having the same sound</i> (e.g. of voc. and nom. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
			</span></i> Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.628
			</span></i>.</div>
